a-j]3
>> =9Anot
>> =9A# mdadm -v --assemble --update=3Drevert-reshape /dev/md3 /dev/sd[=
a-i]3
>
> Yes, my mistake. :-( Try again, including 'sdj3'.
>
> Phil

# mdadm -v --assemble --update=3Drevert-reshape /dev/md3 /dev/sd[a-j]3
mdadm: looking for devices for /dev/md3
mdadm: superblock on /dev/sdj3 doesn't match others - assembly aborted

# mdadm -v --assemble --update=3Drevert-reshape --force /dev/md3 /dev/s=
d[a-j]3
mdadm: looking for devices for /dev/md3
mdadm: superblock on /dev/sdj3 doesn't match others - assembly aborted

Note, that --examine in previous message shows delta devices value "-1"=
 for
all members of array, excepting sdj3, which has value "1", without minu=
s
symbol.

According to mdadm wiki 1.2v superblock placed on device after first 4K=
 and
has size 256 Bytes, plus 2 Bytes per device in the array, in current ca=
se
this is 276 Bytes. Dumping superblock:
# for i in /dev/sd?3; do dd ibs=3D1c skip=3D4000 count=3D276 if=3D$i of=
=3D`echo $i | tr -d /`-superblock.raw; done
# for i in devsd*.raw; do echo -e "\n$i" && hd -v $i; done > superblock=
